{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at exact 53f0e183dd0b2d7a5245e12994231519e7daf02c on request/scope-contract, under promise git:sha1…ba13ae8 on request git:sha1…41d2992\n\nScope and replay contract, revision 12, amended before review, at 53f0e183dd0b2d7a5245e12994231519e7daf02c (two commits on aeda54f7, which no reviewer had claimed). All four subjects; the admission read inventory is unchanged. The amendment makes two decisions that the I2 source work raised, and nothing else. First: a genesis entry states the act kind of its definition's genesis act, as the member kind of the genesis input. The writing scope takes it from its definition; the judge and the replay verifier check it, and a mismatch is the replay result mismatch with the name genesis-kind; a reader of a foreign genesis reads the kind from the entry, with the same trust as any fetched entry. Reason, observed in I2 scenario T3 on real storage (delta DK5): a change lane could not check that a fact names an issue lane's file entry, so the lane forms' common manifest case was refused. Second: a runtime must have code for every capability form the pinned definition uses, or it answers unsupported-definition for the whole scope; a definition that uses only the item form of hold@1 runs where the item form is derived; a scripted capability in tests is a labelled stand-in and proves nothing about the capability. The first amendment commit stated the capability rule by version name, which contradicted section 6.8 and both sources; the second commit corrects it and the corrections file records both wordings. Must-change rows: 10, with 9 owed at a3e5a77e; row 10 (the genesis kind) is owed by the I2 delivery after adoption. New open points R1-48 and R1-49 go to the authority note's owner. Witnesses 18.26 and 18.27 are new. Everything else is as filed at aeda54f7. Reading limit of the amendment: the main note was not read again in full; restatements of the changed rules were found by search on their wording. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"53f0e183dd0b2d7a5245e12994231519e7daf02c","path":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md"}}